  "post-painterly-abstraction": editorialReview("后绘画性抽象约在1950至1960年代以清晰大形、开放色场、薄层综合色和压低个人手势回应抽象表现主义的厚涂与戏剧笔触。", ["open color fields, clearly bounded large shapes, and a suppressed gestural center", "flat contours, long bands or broad color areas, and limited edge variation", "clear saturated color and large continuous layers of one hue", "depth built through color value rather than accumulated paint relief", "thin acrylic, stained canvas, and restrained brush traces", "only when text is requested, use neutral typography outside the color field"]),
  "hard-edge-painting": editorialReview("硬边绘画约在1950至1970年代以锐利遮蔽边缘、封闭综合色块、非透视平衡和无笔触丙烯表面建立比一般几何抽象更明确的综合色边界。", ["large geometric divisions, unequivocal boundaries, and non-perspectival balance", "razor-sharp lines, arcs, and fully closed flat color shapes", "clean saturated color or strong value contrast", "even shadowless illumination with hierarchy created by the color shapes themselves", "smooth acrylic, tape-masked edges, and a brushless surface", "only when text is requested, use minimal legible typography outside the hard-edged field"]),
  "washington-color-school": editorialReview("华盛顿色彩画派约在1950至1970年代以浸染丙烯、裸画布、靶形、条带和透明综合色建立轻薄发光的综合色场，区别于厚重油彩抽象。", ["broad open color fields, centered target structures, or rhythmic vertical bands", "stained soft edges, concentric circles, stripes, and reduced geometry", "bright transparent color with exposed unpainted canvas", "luminosity created by pigment transparency and canvas absorption", "diluted acrylic stain, raw canvas fiber, and no impasto", "only when text is requested, use sparse neutral typography outside the stained field"]),
  "light-and-space": editorialReview("光与空间运动自1960年代在美国西海岸发展，以真实光、感知适应、雾化场域、透明材料和精确观看位置改变空间经验，而非把光仅作为画面效果。", ["precisely controlled openings, perceptual fields, and viewer position within open space", "nearly disappearing boundaries, continuous planes, and perceptual geometry", "white light, spectral color, and extremely low-contrast tonal fields", "light itself acting as material through boundaryless gradients and chromatic adaptation", "glass, resin, fluorescent or projected light, atmospheric haze, and seamless planes", "only when text is requested, use minimal neutral wayfinding typography outside the light field"]),
  "post-minimalism": editorialReview("后极简主义约在1966至1975年让极简重复单元受重力、柔性材料和制作过程改变，以垂坠、卷曲、堆叠和非刚性秩序反对完美工业几何。", ["repeated units altered by gravity, open distribution, and non-rigid order", "sagging, curling, stacking, and process-formed soft geometry", "exposed material color, gray-white, earth tones, and limited pigment", "ambient exhibition light emphasizing gravity and soft real shadows", "felt, rope, latex, fiberglass, and visible process traces", "only when text is requested, keep typography minimal and outside the material process"]),
  "pattern-and-decoration": editorialReview("模式与装饰运动约在1970至1980年代重新肯定满幅纹样、织物、贴片和跨文化装饰传统，以高密度重复和材质愉悦挑战现代主义对装饰的贬抑。", ["all-over pattern, repeated borders, juxtaposed decorative systems, and no dominant center", "floral or geometric motifs, appliqué-like units, and continuous ornamental repetition", "high-saturation multicolor, metallic accents, and strong chromatic contrast", "even pictorial illumination with local material reflection used as rhythm", "textile, collage, ceramic fragments, acrylic, and visibly handmade ornament", "only when text is requested, integrate legible lettering as one controlled pattern layer"]),
